notifications-note = A popup is never raised while this window is the one in front, and a session running no notification server sees none either way. What the desktop draws on one — a cover, the transport buttons, how long it stays — is the server's own to decide.
discord-note = Register an application in Discord's developer portal, name it what the status should say, and paste its application id here. Discord has to be running on this machine: it is told over its own local socket and nothing else is asked.
discord-art-note = A cover is Discord fetching the album's front from the Cover Art Archive by the release's MusicBrainz id, so only a track whose tags or lookup named its release has one. Where none is known the icon stands in — an asset key uploaded to your application, or an image address. No picture on this machine is sent anywhere.
not-an-application = That is not a Discord application id; it is a run of 17 to 20 digits
not-an-icon = An icon is one asset key or one image address, with no spaces
discord-says-only-that-resonate-is = Discord says only that Resonate is running, and nothing of what.
discord-shows-the-title-and-the = Discord shows the title and the artist of what is playing.
discord-shows-the-title-the-artist = Discord shows the title, the artist and the album it is on.
the-albums-cover-from-the-cover = The album's cover from the Cover Art Archive, which Discord fetches itself; nothing on this machine is sent. An album the archive holds none for shows the icon below.
the-icon-named-below-whatever-is = The icon named below, whatever is playing.
no-picture-at-all = No picture at all.
tell-the-desktop-when-a-track = Tell the desktop when a track starts
off-nothing-pops-up-when-the = Off, nothing pops up when the track changes
off-nothing-reaches-discord = Off, nothing reaches Discord
on-and-waiting-for-an-application = On, and waiting for an application id
discord-is-told-what-is-playing = Discord is told what is playing
show-what-is-playing-on-discord = Show what is playing on Discord
application-id = Application id
shows = Shows
picture = Picture
icon = Icon
show-how-far-into-the-track = Show how far into the track
off-no-bar-and-no-time = Off, no bar and no time is drawn
stay-while-paused = Stay while paused
off-the-status-clears-when-the = Off, the status clears when the music pauses
discord-is-told-under-that-application = Discord is told under that application
discord-is-told-nothing-until-an = Discord is told nothing until an application id is given
discord-draws-that-icon-where-no = Discord draws that icon where no cover is known
discord-draws-no-icon = Discord draws no icon
